WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.208
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Welcome to
the Huberman Lab podcast,

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:04.610
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.360
for everyday life.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.090
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.330
I'm Andrew Huberman.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.410
And I'm a professor of
neurobiology and ophthalmology

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.060
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.030
My guests today are Mark
Zuckerberg and Dr. Priscilla

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:18.810
Chan.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.000
Mark Zuckerberg,
as everybody knows,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.620
founded the company Facebook.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.070
He is now the CEO of Meta, which
includes Facebook, Instagram,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.490
WhatsApp, and other
technology platforms.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.009
Dr. Priscilla Chan
graduated from Harvard

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:34.980
and went on to do her medical
degree at the University

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.750
of California San Francisco.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.030
Mark Zuckerberg and
Dr. Priscilla Chan

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.910
are married and the
co-founders of the CZI,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.450
or Chan Zuckerberg Initiative,
a philanthropic organization

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.810
whose stated goal is to
cure all human diseases.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.300
The Chan Zuckerberg Initiative
is accomplishing that

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.390
by providing critical funding
not available elsewhere,

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.970
as well as a novel
framework for discovery

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.430
of the basic
functioning of cells,

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.680
cataloging all the
different human cell

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.129
types, as well as providing
AI, or artificial intelligence,

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:07.020
platforms to mine
all of that data

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.170
to discover new pathways and
cures for all human diseases.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.180
The first hour of
today's discussion

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:16.450
is held with both Dr. Priscilla
Chan and Mark Zuckerberg,

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.480
during which we discuss
the CZI and what it really

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.970
means to try and cure
all human diseases.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.640
We talk about the motivational
backbone for the CZI

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.610
that extends well into each
of their personal histories.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.820
Indeed, you'll learn quite a lot
about Dr. Priscilla Chan, who

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.420
has, I must say, an absolutely
incredible family story leading

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.120
up to her role as a
physician and her motivations

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.740
for the CZI and beyond.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.620
And you'll learn from Mark, how
he is bringing an engineering

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.690
and AI perspective
to the discovery

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.890
of new cures for human disease.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.470
The second half of
today's discussion

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.830
is just between Mark Zuckerberg
and me, during which we discuss

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.210
various Meta Platforms,
including, of course,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.180
social media platforms, and
their effects on mental health

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.430
in children and adults.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.520
We also discuss VR,
Virtual Reality, as well as

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.470
augmented and mixed reality.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.290
And we discuss AI,
Artificial Intelligence,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.650
and how it stands to transform
not just our online experiences

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.750
with social media and
other technologies,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.090
but how it stands to
potentially transform

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.370
every aspect of everyday life.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.260
Before we begin, I'd
like to emphasize

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.840
that this podcast is separate
from my teaching and research

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.870
roles at Stanford.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.870
It is, however, part
of my desire and effort

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.760
to bring zero cost to
consumer information

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.650
about science and
science-related tools

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:27.880
to the general public.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.380
In keeping with
that theme, I'd like

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.940
to thank the sponsors
of today's podcast.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.240
